=== layout: two-panels

# *Percutaneous Umbilical Blood Sampling (PUBS)*

@left

- Percutaneous umbilical blood sampling (PUBS). This is also done in the second trimester using blood removed from the umbilical cord.

@right

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect10d-chromo_aneuploid/image_021.png)

=== layout: two-over-one-panels

# *Newborn Screening*

@top-left

- One common test is for phenylketonuria (PKU)
  - A recessively inherited disorder of phenylalanine metabolism
  - A PKU test is done after a baby is 24 hours old and after the baby has ingested protein to ensure accurate results.

@top-right

![Lecture diagram](assets/lect10d-chromo_aneuploid/image_022.png)

@bottom

- Some genetic disorders can be detected shortly after birth by simple tests that are now routinely performed in most hospitals.
- Blood test results usually are ready by the time a baby is 5&#8211;7 days old. Parents won't often hear about results if screening tests were normal.

=== layout: two-panels
@replaceme

# *Newborn Screening*

@left

- [Metabolic problems.]{color=#168253}
  - phenylketonuria (PKU)
  - methylmalonic acidemia
  - maple syrup urine disease (MSUD)
  - tyrosinemia
  - citrullinema
  - medium chain acyl CoA dehydrogenase (MCAD) deficiency
- [Hemoglobin problems]{color=#F10D0C}
  - sickle cell disease
  - hemoglobin SC disease
  - beta thalassemia

@right

- [Hormone problems.]{color=blue}
  - congenital hypothyroidism
  - congenital adrenal hyperplasia
- [Other problems]{color=#B47804}
  - galactosemia
  - biotidinase deficiency
  - cystic fibrosis
  - severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID)
  - Pompe disease (glycogen storage disease type II)
  - mucopolysaccharidosis type 1
  - X-linked adrenoleukodystropy
  - spinal muscle atrophy (SMA)

=== layout: section

# Nondisjunction

=== layout: one-panel

# *Abnormal Chromosome Number*

@body

- In nondisjunction, pairs of homologous chromosomes do not separate normally during meiosis
- As a result, one gamete receives two of the same type of chromosome, and another gamete receives no copy

