=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Polyploidy changes whole sets; aneuploidy changes chromosome counts.
- Nondisjunction produces gametes with missing or extra chromosomes.
- Trisomy 21 involves an extra copy of chromosome 21.
- Screening estimates risk; diagnostic testing examines fetal material.

